undo-tree-mode replaces the standard Emacs undo system with one that
treats undo history as what it is: a branching tree of changes.  It
combines the intuitive behavior of a conventional undo/redo system with
the ability to recover any past state of a buffer, without ever losing
history.

The undo tree can be visualized and navigated in a separate buffer,
and history can optionally be saved to and restored from disk.
